{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P26692", "uniProtkbId": "ACDA_METSH", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1992-08-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2025-04-09", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1992-08-01", "entryVersion": 120, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 3.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Methanothrix soehngenii", "commonName": "Methanosaeta concilii", "taxonId": 2223, "lineage": ["Archaea", "Methanobacteriati", "Methanobacteriota", "Stenosarchaea group", "Methanomicrobia", "Methanotrichales", "Methanotrichaceae", "Methanothrix"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "Acetyl-CoA decarbonylase/synthase complex subunit alpha"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "ACDS complex subunit alpha"}], "ecNumbers": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "1.2.7.4"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "ACDS complex carbon monoxide dehydrogenase subunit alpha"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "ACDS CODH subunit alpha"}]}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "cdhA"}}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "Part of the ACDS complex that catalyzes the reversible cleavage of acetyl-CoA, allowing autotrophic growth from CO(2). The alpha-epsilon subcomponent functions as a carbon monoxide dehydrogenase"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "CO + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + H2O = 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]-[ferredoxin] + CO2 + 2 H(+)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:21040"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:10000"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:10001"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15377"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15378"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:16526"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:17245"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:33737"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:33738"}], "ecNumber": "1.2.7.4", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}]}}, {"commentType": "COFACTOR", "cofactors": [{"name": "[4Fe-4S] cluster", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:49883"}}], "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Binds 6 [4Fe-4S] clusters per heterotetramer."}]}}, {"commentType": "COFACTOR", "cofactors": [{"name": "[Ni-4Fe-4S] cluster", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:47739"}}], "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "Binds 2 [Ni-4Fe-4S] clusters per heterotetramer."}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "Heterotetramer of two alpha and two epsilon subunits. The ACDS complex is made up of alpha, epsilon, beta, gamma and delta subunits with a probable stoichiometry of (alpha(2)epsilon(2))(4)-beta(8)-(gamma(1)delta(1))(8)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "Cluster B is an all-cysteinyl-liganded 4Fe-4S cluster; cluster C is a mixed Ni-Fe-S cluster which is the active site of CO oxidation. Cluster D is also an all-cysteinyl-liganded 4Fe-4S cluster that bridges the two subunits of the CODH dimer. Contains two additional 4Fe-4S clusters, dubbed E and F, that probably transport electrons from ferredoxin to the B cluster"}], "commentType": "DOMAIN"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "value": "Belongs to the Ni-containing carbon monoxide dehydrogenase family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "This protein lacks the conserved Cys in positions 52 and 56; they are replaced by an Asp and a Thr, respectively. It is therefore possible that the D-cluster is either altered or missing in this protein, which may not form heterotetramers"}], "commentType": "CAUTION"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 793, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Acetyl-CoA decarbonylase/synthase complex subunit alpha", "featureId": "PRO_0000155082"}, {"type": "Domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 393, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 422, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "4Fe-4S ferredoxin-type 1", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}]}, {"type": "Domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 432, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 461, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "4Fe-4S ferredoxin-type 2", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}]}, {"type": "Binding site", "location": {"start": {"value": 55, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 55, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "", "featureCrossReferences": [{"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:49883"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_01137"}], "ligand": {"name": "[4Fe-4S] cluster", "id": "ChEBI:CHEBI:49883", "label": "2"}}, {"typ